        answer: "Wallach's core reframing of nutrition: your health is determined not by what you eat but by what you actually absorb. He calls the familiar adage 'you are what you eat' inaccurate and replaces it with 'you are what you absorb' -- the foundation of his two-pronged model, in which supplying the 90 essential nutrients only works if the gut is healthy enough to take them up.",
        verbatim: "There is an old adage that states \u201Cyou are what you eat.\u201D Unfortunately, this old\nadage is not correct. It is more correct and accurate to say \u201Cyou are what you\nabsorb.\u201D",
        page: 596,
