        answer: "The scale of U.S. water fluoridation and its trade-off. About 10,000 American towns and cities \u2014 serving 100 million people \u2014 add fluoride to municipal drinking water at 1 mg/L (one part per million), which has reportedly cut dental cavities by 60 to 70%. But in certain western U.S. states there is an excess of fluoride \u2014 10 to 45 ppm \u2014 with the visible result of mottled (fluorosis-stained) teeth in children.",
